# Production is always Access-authenticated. Never expose local mode via tunnel.
DASHBOARD_MODE=hosted
PORT=4317
DASHBOARD_ORIGIN=https://dashboard.YOUR_DOMAIN
CF_ACCESS_TEAM=https://YOUR_TEAM.cloudflareaccess.com
CF_ACCESS_AUD=YOUR_ACCESS_APPLICATION_AUDIENCE
DASHBOARD_OWNER=YOUR_EMAIL
# The immutable release identity: release.json inside the release directory (default), or an
# absolute path. Hosted mode refuses to start without a valid manifest. Generate it per release:
# {"version":"0.1.0","releaseId":"release-2026-01-01","schemaId":"pilot-state-1","createdAt":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"}
# DASHBOARD_RELEASE_MANIFEST=/home/USER/.local/share/pilot-releases/current/release.json
# Persistent data and approved roots are separate from application releases.
DASHBOARD_DATA=/home/USER/.local/share/pilot
DASHBOARD_ROOTS=/home/USER/projects
# Optional explicitly provided registry snapshot; no live Mac filesystem access.
# DASHBOARD_REGISTRY=/approved/path/projects.json
# Agent harness file-edit capability (default: off). Set to 'on' to enable the bounded file-edit tool
# so agents with the file_edit scope can propose or apply edits. Even when enabled, the default mode
# is propose-only (no file is written) unless the acceptance policy permits auto-apply.
# DASHBOARD_FILE_EDIT=on

# Local release capabilities (default: off). `deploy` promotes the project's configured built artifact
# into one owner-configured local directory and keeps the previous generation for manual rollback;
# `publish` copies an exact, bounded set of reviewed files into one owner-configured publication root.
# Both are local filesystem targets, not Cloudflare or CI providers, and both still require the
# agent's deploy/publish scope, a bound agent and the acceptance policy's full-auto decision.
# DASHBOARD_DEPLOY=on
# DASHBOARD_PUBLISH=on


# Enable the agent commit tool (default: off). Set to 'on' to install `commit_preview` and
# `commit_accepted` for agents with the commit scope, with a control store, an owner-configured
# commit target and an agent-may-accept policy whose commit decision is full-auto. It commits the
# exact staged tree to the fixed Pilot branch and never pushes; staging is not secret scanning.
# DASHBOARD_AGENT_COMMIT=on
# Enable the agent push tool (default: off). Set to 'on' to install `push_preview` and
# `push_accepted` for agents with the push scope, with a control store, an owner-configured push
# target and the same full-auto policy requirement. It pushes one accepted commit, without force,
# to one locally configured filesystem remote; there is no hosted credential integration.
# DASHBOARD_AGENT_PUSH=on

# Enable the owner-only Cloudflare connection configuration route (default: off). It stores one
# unencrypted credential in credentials/ and performs no provider request or deployment; revoking
# it here does not revoke the token at Cloudflare. See docs/specs/cloudflare-connection-store.md.
# DASHBOARD_CLOUDFLARE_CONNECTION=on

# Enable the local test-execution capability (default off). With this on, a named agent bound to a
# session and granted the run_tests scope can run the fixed `node --test` recipe in the registered
# project root. It runs as the application user inside the application container and is NOT a
# sandbox: the tests can read credentials/, the durable control store and every project, and can
# modify this project. There are no cgroup memory or PID limits, and stopping a run is a best-effort
# process-group signal. See docs/RUNNER.md.
# DASHBOARD_TEST_RUNNER=on

# Enable the opt-in reusable JSON projection tools (default: off). An owner must also grant the
# 'reusable_tools' scope to a bound named agent. Definitions are bounded data, never code, and
# nothing is executed. See docs/specs/reusable-json-tools.md.
# DASHBOARD_REUSABLE_TOOLS=on

# Enable the installed provisioning tool (default: off). A bound named agent also needs the
# 'provision' scope and an acceptance under an agent-may-accept policy with provision=full-auto.
# The tool creates one Pilot-owned local directory with a bounded manifest under this approved root;
# the root must be a real directory that overlaps neither the data root nor a registered project.
# See "Installed spend and provision tools" in docs/AGENTS.md.
# DASHBOARD_PROVISION_ACTIONS=on
# DASHBOARD_PROVISION_ROOT=/home/USER/.local/share/pilot-provisioned

# Enable the installed metered spend tool (default: off). A bound named agent also needs the 'spend'
# scope and an acceptance under an agent-may-accept policy with spend=full-auto. The bearer token is
# read from DASHBOARD_DATA/credentials/spend-billing.json (private, mode 0600); it is never returned
# to a model. Caps are hard limits on what Pilot sends, not a global or provider-side spending limit.
# See "Installed spend and provision tools" in docs/AGENTS.md.
# DASHBOARD_SPEND_ACTIONS=on
# DASHBOARD_SPEND_BILLING_URL=https://billing.example.test/charge
# DASHBOARD_SPEND_ACCOUNT_ID=YOUR_BILLING_ACCOUNT
# DASHBOARD_SPEND_CURRENCY=USD
# DASHBOARD_SPEND_PROJECT_CAP_MINOR=5000
# DASHBOARD_SPEND_CHARGE_CAP_MINOR=500
# DASHBOARD_SPEND_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
